      "description": "Scope and shading switches.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-seg\" role=\"radiogroup\"><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"true\">Week</button><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\">Day</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-seg{display:inline-flex;height:44px;padding:2px;border-radius:0.75rem;background:var(--color-surface-2)}.ds-seg button{flex:1;padding:0 12px;border:0;border-radius:calc(0.75rem - 2px);background:transparent;color:var(--color-ink-2);font:500 .8125rem/1.125rem system-ui,sans-serif;transition:background-color .15s,color .15s,box-shadow .15s;cursor:pointer}.ds-seg button:hover{color:var(--color-ink)}.ds-seg button[aria-checked=\"true\"]{background:var(--color-thumb);color:var(--color-ink);box-shadow:var(--shadow-thumb,0 1px 2px oklch(0.2 0.015 260 / .14),0 2px 6px -2px oklch(0.2 0.015 260 / .12))}.ds-seg button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sets Stepper",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "stepper-button",
      "description": "Hard sets per entry.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-step\"><button aria-label=\"Fewer\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"/></svg></button><div class=\"ds-step-v\"><b>3</b><small>sets</small></div><button aria-label=\"More\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M5 12h14M12 5v14\"/></svg></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-step{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px}.ds-step button{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:36px;height:36px;border:0;border-radius:9999px;background:var(--color-surface-2);color:var(--color-ink);transition:background-color .15s,scale .15s;cursor:pointer}.ds-step button:hover{background:var(--color-line)}.ds-step button:active{scale:.9}.ds-step button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.ds-step-v{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;min-width:40px;line-height:1;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--color-ink);font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-step-v b{font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:600}.ds-step-v small{margin-top:2px;font-size:.6875rem;color:var(--color-ink-3)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Search Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "Borderless well input; focus is the global cobalt ring.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search exercises\">",
      "css": ".ds-input{height:44px;width:280px;padding:0 12px;border:0;border-radius:0.75rem;background:var(--color-surface-2);color:var(--color-ink);font:400 1rem/1.375rem system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--color-ink-3)}.ds-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Coverage Panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Flat panel with a display number and hairline rows.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><p class=\"ds-big\"><b>15</b> <span>of 19</span></p><p class=\"ds-cap\">groups trained</p><ul><li><span>Chest</span><span>12 sets</span></li><li><span>Lats</span><span>9 sets</span></li></ul></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{width:320px;padding:16px;border-radius:1.25rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-ink);font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-big{margin:0}.ds-big b{font:600 2.75rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.01em}.ds-big span{font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-ink-3)}.ds-cap{margin:4px 0 12px;font-size:.8125rem;color:var(--color-ink-2)}.ds-panel ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.ds-panel li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-line);font-size:1rem}.ds-panel li span:last-child{color:var(--color-ink-2)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tab Bar",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab-bar",
      "description": "Phone bottom navigation; current tab in cobalt.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabs\"><a aria-current=\"page\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 9h18M8 2v4M16 2v4\"/></svg>Plan</a><a><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M12 8v7M7 11h10M9 22l3-7 3 7\"/></svg>Body</a><a><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"><path d=\"M6 6v12M18 6v12M3 9v6M21 9v6M6 12h12\"/></svg>Exercises</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:flex;width:360px;height:56px;padding:0 8px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-line);background:color-mix(in oklab,var(--color-canvas) 90%,transparent);backdrop-filter:saturate(1.4) blur(20px)}.ds-tabs a{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:2px;color:var(--color-ink-3);font:500 .6875rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer;transition:color .15s}.ds-tabs a:hover{color:var(--color-ink-2)}.ds-tabs a[aria-current=\"page\"]{color:var(--color-accent)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Calibrated Instrument",
    "overview": "Tenset is a measuring tool for a training week. The chrome is quiet graphite, cool and nearly colorless, so that the cobalt volume scale on the body map reads as data and nothing else. Exercises carry a second, categorical voice: a soft pastel per movement group, so a day or a week shows its balance at a glance. Numbers are the product: they are big, condensed, tabular and always paired with the words that explain them. The interface behaves like a well-made gauge: exact, legible at arm's length in a gym, and silent about what it does not know.\n\nDensity is phone-first and calm: one 640 px column, grouped panels on a slightly darker canvas, hairline rows inside panels instead of nested cards. On desktop the same system widens into a week board with a nav rail and a sticky map panel; it never gains decoration in exchange for space. Recovery and volume are stated, never judged, so no color ever means \"warning\", and Tailwind's default palette is removed on purpose.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Graphite neutrals with a faint cool tint (hue 260) in both themes.",
      "Cobalt is the brand, the only volume hue, and (one step deeper) the interactive accent.",
      "Movement groups get categorical pastels on exercise surfaces, always with dark mv-ink text and a text label.",
      "Primary actions are ink, not color.",
      "System fonts for now; big numbers use font-num at 600.",
      "Tabular figures everywhere.",
      "Flat panels; shadows only on things that float.",
      "Light and dark themes are first-class, each tuned on its own."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Volume is the only color on the body map and volume legends. Movement groups get categorical pastels on exercise surfaces only, always with mv-ink text and a text label, never on volume data. Color is never the only cue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Alarm Rule",
        "body": "No warning semantics, in either theme. No color ever means \"too much\", \"risk\" or \"too soon\"; the movement pastels are categories, not states. Bands are words in neutral pills. The default Tailwind palette stays removed.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Action Rule",
        "body": "Primary buttons are ink on on-ink. Cobalt marks interactivity (links, focus, current tab), never the main call to action fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number is tabular (font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums on body, num utility for emphasis), so stepping 9 → 10 sets never shifts a column.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Condensed Is For Numbers Rule",
        "body": "font-num sets numerals only. Words, units and labels stay in font-sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Panels Don't Float Rule",
        "body": "Panels and cards never carry a shadow. If something has a shadow, it is above the page and can be dismissed.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the vol-* scale for volume and nothing else.",
      "Do color exercise surfaces by movement group (bg-mv-<group> with text-mv-ink) and always show the group or exercise name with it.",
      "Do put thumbnails on white inside a group-colored ring or frame.",
      "Do make the primary action ink (bg-ink text-on-ink); keep accent for links, focus and the current tab.",
      "Do set big numbers as font-num text-display font-semibold, followed by a unit in ink-2 or ink-3.",
      "Do keep every number tabular.",
      "Do group content in flat surface panels at 1.25rem with hairline rows inside.",
      "Do give every target a 44 px hit area (hit utility for smaller visuals).",
      "Do check each new token or surface in both light and dark themes; the dark values are tuned, not inverted."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a warning color or any color that means a state (too much, too soon, risk), in either theme, for any reason.",
      "Don't put movement colors on the body map, volume legends, bands or volume numbers.",
      "Don't tint the figure or use mix-blend-mode on thumbnails; the owner rejected the purple-tinted figure.",
      "Don't use ink or ink-2 text on a pastel fill; use mv-ink, which stays dark in dark mode.",
      "Don't color volume bands. Bands are words in neutral pills.",
      "Don't put a shadow on a panel or card.",
      "Don't fill a primary button with cobalt.",
      "Don't use font-num for words, or a light weight for big numbers.",
      "Don't reintroduce warm cream surfaces or brass accents; the owner retired that look as an AI default.",
      "Don't load fonts, textures or icons from a third-party origin; everything is self-hosted.",
      "Don't nest cards inside panels."
    ]
  }
}
